 "text": "9/29/26, 10:16 AM\nUsing the submission run is recommended if you are processing large volumes of data.\n\nActivities\n\n1. On the SAP Easy Access screen, choose |/*Periodic Processing \u00bb For Contract Accounts \u00bb Submission for Collection\nSubmission Run 3 (transaction FPQ3DM).\n\n2. Enter a date and an ID that you can use to identify the run later.\n\n3. Restrict the selection of items to be submitted on the General Selections tab by business partner, contract account, and/or\n\ncompany code. On the Additional Selection tab page, you can refine even further the selection of the items to be\nsubmitted.\n\n4. lf you set the relevant indicators on the Submission Parameters tab, you can also submit items that have been written off\nand items that have been posted statistically. If you set the indicator Submit Additional Items, in addition to the items\nreleased for collection, you can also submit all additional items of the business partner (See Submitting Receivables to\n\nCollection Agencies).\n\nIf you work with debt recovery scores, you can enter a variant for checking the debt recovery score when you submit items.\n5. Choose the collection agency that you want to submit the receivables to.\n\nFor submitting using files, to create a submission file, select the corresponding indicator and define a path under which the\nfile is saved. If you set the indicator Payment Form ID for Collection Agency, all items submitted for a business partner are\ngrouped under a payment form ID that the collection agency can specify as a payment reference in its report. If you set the\nindicator Total Receivables to be Submitted, the items in the file are totaled by contract account, business partner, or\npayment form.\n\nFor submission via Enterprise Service/API, during an update run, the system automatically sends the data relevant for\nsubmission to the collection agency using Enterprise Services.\n\n6. Schedule the program run. For more information, see Functions for Scheduling Program Runs.\n\nThe submission run records all submissions in logs. To ease the load on your system, you can delete these logs. To do this, on the\nSAP Easy Access screen, choose |)\u00bbPeriodic Processing \u00bb Delete Data \u00bb Logs of Submissions for Collection 3 (transaction\nFPO3DML).\n",
